- From karaoke joints, to quirky
shops, to Korean barbecue,

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.390
Koreatown is quickly becoming

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:22.700
one of L.A.'s most popular neighborhoods.

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:24.740
So I'm here hanging out with--

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:26.640
- [Unison] NCT 127!

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:28.060
♪ I'm the biggest hit ♪

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.240
♪ I'm the biggest hit on the stage ♪

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:33.740
- [Rich] This is NCT 127,
Korea's new hottest K-pop band.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:35.040
- I'm Taeyong.
- Haechan.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:35.910
- Mark.
- Jaehyun.

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:36.830
- I'm Winwin.
- Doyoung.

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:37.780
- Taeil.
- Johnny.

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:38.693
- I'm Yuta. (blows kiss)

00:00:38.693 --> 00:00:39.790
- And my name's Rich.

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:43.510
In case you didn't know,
NCT 127 is a big deal.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:46.510
Not only do they have millions
of fans all over the world,

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:49.090
they are number two on
Billboard's Social Chart.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:51.020
That's above Bieber and Beyonce.

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:54.140
They live together, travel
together, and rehearse together.

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:55.570
They even hang out together.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:57.870
We decided to meet to have Korean barbecue

00:00:57.950 --> 00:00:59.660
at Quarters on 6th Avenue.

00:00:59.961 --> 00:01:02.378
(rock music)

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:06.770
So I'm originally from London,

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:09.100
and I didn't even know
what Korean barbecue was.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:10.790
- Wait, this is your first time eating--

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:12.740
- It's like my third time.
- Oh, your third time.

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:14.790
- This is pretty much how it
looks like in Korea as well.

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:16.340
- You can't change it much, right?

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:17.780
It is what it is.
- It is what it is.

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:18.613
- Yeah.

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:20.790
- It's just meat, and
you barbecue it. (laughs)

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:21.800
- Yeah, you just grill it.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:23.430
This is my first time eating
it with cheese, though.

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:25.730
- Americans love cheese,
cheese on everything.

00:01:26.443 --> 00:01:28.860
(rock music)

00:01:30.746 --> 00:01:32.526
- Oh, this is, do you know
what kinda water this is?

00:01:32.526 --> 00:01:33.359
- [Rich] What?

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:34.192
- [Mark] It's like tea.

00:01:34.192 --> 00:01:35.025
- Oh, it is?

00:01:35.025 --> 00:01:35.858
- I think it's called boricha.

00:01:35.858 --> 00:01:36.691
- Cheers, everyone.

00:01:36.691 --> 00:01:37.530
- [Unison] Cheers.

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:40.064
- Water cheers, water cheers.

00:01:40.064 --> 00:01:41.490
(cheering and laughing)

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:42.677
- [Rich] So what're we gonna have?

00:01:42.677 --> 00:01:44.250
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:46.200
- Wanna just order a large, or a combo?

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:47.760
- Whatever you guys want.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:49.870
Are you guys hungry, or not really?

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:50.993
- Hungry!

00:01:51.326 --> 00:01:53.500
