00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:56.900
pork chow, kalbi beef, and
a hundred other things.

00:01:57.810 --> 00:01:59.410
So what are all the things we've got here?

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:01.450
- This is, like, a pancake.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:02.283
- [Rich] Kimchi pancake.

00:02:02.283 --> 00:02:03.760
- With vegetables and kimchi.

00:02:04.917 --> 00:02:05.980
It's actually really traditional.

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:07.330
- All right, so I'll try some.

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:08.580
I'm really bad with chopsticks.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:10.450
I'm really bad with chopsticks,

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:13.737
I might need to ask for a fork.

00:02:13.737 --> 00:02:14.570
(all laugh)

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:15.910
- I don't even know how to do it.

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:17.654
- I'll cut.
(all laugh)

00:02:17.654 --> 00:02:18.487
- Show me how to do it.

00:02:18.487 --> 00:02:20.270
Oh, you do the spread?
- Yeah.

00:02:20.932 --> 00:02:23.740
(poppy synth music)

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:24.573
- Thanks, man.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:26.210
- [Mark] You should
ask for a fork, though.

00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:28.400
- No, I'm gonna persevere,
I'm gonna try it.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:31.400
(poppy synth music)

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:32.573
- Oh, it's good.

00:02:35.586 --> 00:02:36.850
- He says that he can
really make that well.

00:02:37.208 --> 00:02:38.358
- You can do this well?

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:39.690
Yeah, you're gonna flip them?

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:41.030
Nice.
(all laugh)

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:45.030
So what do you think has, like,
made K-pop as big as it is?

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:47.006
'Cause it's just getting
bigger and bigger and bigger.

00:02:47.006 --> 00:02:49.252
(singing in foreign language)

00:02:49.252 --> 00:02:51.752
♪ Cherry bomb ♪

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:54.280
- America itself is accepting K-pop

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:55.700
more and more comfortably now.

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:58.150
K-pop, like, the NCT music
is actually really similar

00:02:58.150 --> 00:02:59.670
to pop music in America as well.

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:00.800
- Yeah.
- The beats and stuff.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.270
And there are actually American writers

00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:03.650
who write our songs as well.
- Oh, that's cool.

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:06.550
- And so I think the
listeners are more familiar

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:09.460
with the beats if they like
American music as well,

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:11.290
'cause they always like
what's familiar to them.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:12.123
- Yeah.

00:03:12.123 --> 00:03:13.660
And your fan base is NCTzens?

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:15.310
- [All] Yeah! (cheer)

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:16.705
